{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>וַיִּנָּחֶם ה׳.</b> Meaning, He relented for two reasons: the first, because the thing was evil; the second, because it was evil directed at His nation." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend along this line — <b>and He relented concerning the evil that He had spoken</b> — specifically with regard to the speech, but had He sworn, then not." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend that He relented only concerning the evil that He had spoken — that is, to annihilate them — but there yet remains another evil concerning which He did not relent, namely the evil consequences that the calf brought about, as is known." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend that He relented only concerning the evil that He had spoken to do to those who did not sin, who are reckoned by the name of His nation; but as for those who worshipped idolatry, whether with witnesses or without witnesses, but in their hearts they believed in it — their evil stood against them: from among them ה׳ smote, etc., and from among them Moses put to the sword, and from among them the sons of Levi struck them down."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:35:59.143833078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}